IMU daemon — attitude, heading, and heave for boats ("gpsd for IMUs")
 imud reads an I2C IMU and magnetometer, fuses them with a quaternion
 Multiplicative EKF, and serves attitude, heading (magnetic and WMM true),
 rate of turn, and heave to the network: NMEA 0183 over UDP, a high-rate
 binary UDP stream, and a local AF_UNIX subscription socket.
 .
 Includes calibration (imud-cal), status and monitoring tools (imud-status,
 imud-mon), C and Python client libraries, and a hardened systemd service.
 Optional protocol bridges are packaged separately: imud-signalk, imud-mqtt,
 imud-influxdb, imud-mavlink.
